+// Returns a size scaled down below the `xl` boundary by the release's responsive font size rule,
+// with its 1.25rem floor and its factor of 10. A zero-width viewport resolves the floor plus a
+// tenth of the size's excess over it, the other nine tenths of the excess return in proportion to
+// the viewport width, and the whole size is back at the boundary. The `max()` guard leaves a size
+// at or under the floor fixed at every viewport, so a size token retuned across the floor switches
+// between the fluid and the fixed behavior at runtime. The boundary is interpolated, because Sass
+// would otherwise divide the viewport length by it and refuse the result.
+@function fluid-size($size) {
+	@return calc($size - max($size * 0.9 - 1.125rem, 0px) * (1 - 100vw / #{breakpoint(xl)}));
+}
+
+// Emits a `font-size` declaration of the value the `fluid-size` function returns for `$size`, and
+// the size itself from the `xl` boundary on, as the release's `font-size` mixin does. At the
+// boundary the fluid value equals the size, so the cap meets it without a jump.
+@mixin font-size($size) {
+	font-size: fluid-size($size);
+	@include breakpoint-up(xl) {
+		font-size: $size;
+	}
+}
+
 // Returns the WCAG 2.2 relative luminance of a color given as its channel triplet, each channel
 // from 0 to 255.
 @function luminance($triplet) {
